<article>
	<h1><span>Private Messages: Messages</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#filters">Filters</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists the private messages sent to you. Messages sent to other people are not shown.</p>
		<p>Click a message's <strong>Subject</strong> to read it.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="filters">
		<h2><span>Filters</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Filter:</dt>
			<dd>A text box (with the placeholder <em>Search in message subject or description</em>) and
				<strong>Search</strong> and <strong>Clear</strong> buttons.</dd>

			<dt>- Select Status -</dt>
			<dd>A drop-down with <em>Read</em>, <em>Unread</em> and <em>Trashed</em>. Without a choice the list
				shows read and unread messages.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>
		<p>Click a column heading to sort the list by that column.</p>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more messages. To select all messages, check the box in the column
				heading. After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected
				messages.</dd>

			<dt>Subject</dt>
			<dd>The subject of the message. Click it to read the message.</dd>

			<dt>Read</dt>
			<dd>Whether you have read the message: <em>Read</em> or <em>Unread</em>.
				If you may change message states, click the marker to switch it.</dd>

			<dt>From</dt>
			<dd>The name of the person who sent the message.</dd>

			<dt>Date</dt>
			<dd>The date and time the message was sent.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>New</dt>
			<dd>Opens the screen to write a new private message.</dd>

			<dt>Mark As Read</dt>
			<dd>Marks the selected messages as read.</dd>

			<dt>Mark as Unread</dt>
			<dd>Marks the selected messages as unread.</dd>

			<dt>Trash</dt>
			<dd>Shown in place of <strong>Empty trash</strong> unless the list is showing trashed messages.
				Moves the selected messages to the trash.</dd>

			<dt>Empty trash</dt>
			<dd>Shown when the list is showing trashed messages. Permanently deletes the selected messages.</dd>

			<dt>My Settings</dt>
			<dd>Opens a pop-up window with your own messaging settings: <em>Lock Inbox</em>,
				<em>Email New Messages</em> and <em>Auto-purge Messages (days)</em>.</dd>

			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the component's options, which hold its permissions.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
		<p><strong>New</strong> is shown only to users who may create messages. <strong>Mark As Read</strong>,
			<strong>Mark as Unread</strong> and <strong>Trash</strong> are shown only to users who may change
			message states. <strong>Empty trash</strong> is shown only to users who may delete messages.
			<strong>Options</strong> is shown only to users who may configure the component.</p>
	</section>
</article>
